# Deterministic bytes on every platform.
#
# Windows checkouts default to core.autocrlf=true, which would rewrite tracked LF files
# to CRLF on checkout. Two properties here depend on the checked-out bytes:
#
#   1. The report templates are compared byte-for-byte against golden fixtures, and the
#      renderer injects finding blocks joined with '\n'. A CRLF template therefore yields
#      mixed-EOL output that matches no golden on any platform.
#   2. The release ZIP hashes tracked file bytes, so a CRLF checkout produces a different
#      package sha256 than the same commit built on Linux or macOS.
#
# Every tracked file in this repository is text and none contains CRLF, so pinning eol=lf
# changes nothing in-repo — it only stops the checkout from introducing a platform variant.
* text=auto eol=lf
